        ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,E=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices."
